156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (Why Combine Context API and useReducer?)
/E (Why Combine Context API and useReducer?)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
157 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 547 0 R
/ActualText (Using the Context API alone works well for sharing state across components, but managing complex state transitions can become cumbersome. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
158 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 548 0 R
/ActualText (The useReducer hook simplifies this by encapsulating the logic of state transitions, making your code more predictable and easier to debug.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
159 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 549 0 R
/ActualText (When you combine them:)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
160 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 550 0 R
/ActualText (Context API provides the mechanism to share state globally.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
161 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 551 0 R
/ActualText (useReducer manages complex state transitions in a structured way.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
162 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 552 0 R
/ActualText (This combination allows you to scale state management without adding complexity.)
/Pg 10 0 R
