>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 553 0 R
/ActualText (1. Centralized state management:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 554 0 R
/ActualText (By combining Context API and Reducers, you can manage your application's state from a single source. This eliminates the need for "prop drilling," where props are passed through many layers of components.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 555 0 R
/ActualText (2. Predictable state updates:)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 556 0 R
/ActualText (Using a Reducer ensures that state changes happen in a predictable and controlled manner. Reducers are pure functions that take the current state and an action to return the new state. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 557 0 R
/ActualText ( This predictable pattern makes it easier to follow and understand how the state is updated, reducing potential errors or unexpected changes.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (@oluwakemi Oluwadahunsi)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 126 0 R
/Pg 12 0 R
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 558 0 R
/ActualText (3. Easier debugging and testing:)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 559 0 R
/ActualText (With Reducers, state updates become easier to trace and test since they follow a consistent structure. Each action leads to a well-defined state transition, making it straightforward to debug state changes and test the behavior of your application in isolation.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 560 0 R
/ActualText (4. No need for additional libraries:)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 561 0 R
/ActualText (The combination of Context API and Reducers provides a built-in, lightweight alternative to Redux. While Redux is a robust tool, for smaller applications, this method allows you to manage global state without the need for external libraries, keeping your project simpler and easier to maintain.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
